# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# The release image in Dockerfile reads go.mod, go.sum, cmd and internal, and the
# Complement image in deploy/complement/Dockerfile copies the repository to build the
# same module. Either way, everything else here is either evidence or runtime state:
# a docs tree that changes the layer hash for no reason, a test suite that nothing in
# the image runs, or a database, key or log that would be published as an image layer
# if it were copied in.
.git
.github
.agent-work
docs
tests
README.md
AGENTS.md
Makefile
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
LICENSE

# Runtime state and secrets. Never in an image, never one COPY away from one.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
.env
.env.*
/data/
/media/
/tmp/
/secrets/
*.log

# Build and test leftovers.
bin/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.test
*.out
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
